{"title":"The Art and Craft of Problem Solving","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1119239907/artofproblems-20\">The Art and Craft of Problem Solving</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Paul_Zeitz\" title=\"Paul Zeitz\">Paul Zeitz</a>, former coach of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=U.S._IMO\" title=\"U.S. IMO\">U.S. IMO</a> team, is generally thought of as a good mathematical book for when one is finished with the Art of Problem Solving.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Art_and_Craft_of_Problem_Solving&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Resources for mathematics competitions\">Resources for mathematics competitions</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=The_Art_and_Craft_of_Problem_Solving&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018111934\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 11/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 349/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.304      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.304      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Save